/// The room rows of one parent, for the calls integration: open rooms of one key -- a key opens few rooms at a time, capped by the policy. actor.userId scoping is not the fix: the calls integration runs as the site owner or the cluster, so a caller term would decide nothing, and what @serverOnly withholds is the WIRE.
@serverOnly
@unbounded("open rooms of one key -- a key opens few rooms at a time, capped by the policy")
@actor
@cache(0)
query room callsOpenRoomsForKey {
  args {
    keyId  string!
  }
  filter  row => row.keyId == args.keyId && isOpen(row) && (row.ownerUserId == actor.userId || actor.isClusterOwner == true)
  shape   callsRoomFull
}

/// The open rooms placed on one media server, whichever deployable each is for: a server's seats are shared by every call on it, so its free seats are counted across all of them (integrations/calls rooms.go). Read as the cluster acting. It requires an open room, so it starts from the lookup index of the versions written while a room was open, and an ended room leaves that index once its superseded versions expire, a day after it ended (v1:calls:room @retention): it reads the server's open rooms and the rooms open on it within the last day. actor.userId scoping is not the fix: the calls integration runs as the site owner or the cluster, so a caller term would decide nothing, and what @serverOnly withholds is the WIRE.
@serverOnly
@unbounded("open rooms of one media server -- bounded by how many calls the server's seats can carry")
@actor
@cache(0)
query room callsOpenRoomsOnServer {
  args {
    mediaServerId  string!
  }
  filter  row => row.mediaServerId == args.mediaServerId && isOpen(row) && (row.ownerUserId == actor.userId || actor.isClusterOwner == true)
  shape   callsRoomFull
}

/// One seat row by its own id. The calls integration reads it before it writes, and to answer a request that names it. actor.userId scoping is not the fix: the calls integration runs as the site owner or the cluster, so a caller term would decide nothing, and what @serverOnly withholds is the WIRE.
@serverOnly
@unbounded("seat by id -- bounded to a single row (id is the row's own primary key)")
